Patch-Id: ASTRA-0014
Title: Astra platform passkeys (software WebAuthn authenticator + encrypted vault)
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: dom/webauthn/authrs_bridge/Cargo.toml, dom/webauthn/authrs_bridge/src/lib.rs, dom/webauthn/components.conf, dom/webauthn/moz.build, modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml, toolkit/modules/WebAuthnPromptHelper.sys.mjs, Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml
Intent: Linux has no platform authenticator, so `WebAuthnService.h` falls back to `authrs_bridge`, which only spoke USB; every resident-key or user-verification request ended at "Touch your security key". This adds a CTAP2.1 `internal` platform token backed by `astra_passkeys` (toolkit/components/astra_passkeys, staged from passkeys/engine): ES256 credentials sealed at rest with AES-256-CBC + HMAC-SHA256 (encrypt-then-MAC) from NSS, a vault key wrapped by PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256-600k over the CTAP2 PIN hash (the same value ClientPIN transmits, so the WebAuthn path never sees the plaintext PIN twice), `alwaysUv`, system authentication (fprintd) with PIN fallback, persisted rate limits, and a per-transaction lock. `nsIAstraPasskeys` is the Settings seam (status/create/unlock/lock/change PIN/system unlock/list/remove), registered as `@astra/passkeys;1`. `WebAuthnPromptHelper` stands its native doorhanger down when `astra.passkeys.ui` is true so Astra's sheet answers. A request that is not a passkey request still uses the USB path, and a private browsing context is cancelled at the prompt seam before the token can act.
Risk: medium (new WebAuthn transport and a credential store; the token is only offered when the vault exists and the `security.webauthn.astra_passkeys` pref is on, USB keeps working for non-passkey requests, and the at-rest format fails closed on any MAC mismatch)
Test: `passkeys/engine` cargo test 16/16 (PBKDF2 vectors, seal tamper, lockout, device unlock, PIN change, corrupt file); `tests/contract/passkeys_model.mjs` 19/19; `wire_coverage.mjs` 51/51; `check-drift.sh` clean; `tools/marionette-probe/passkeys-probe.py` 24/24 on the packaged dev build (create, platform attachment + internal transport, sign in, wrong PIN + retries, browser-wide switch, UVPAA false when off, vault 0600 and no PIN/RP in clear, one credential listed)
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: delete the pref + component + IDL and drop `astra_passkeys` from gkrust; the vault file is inert without the token. If upstream gains a Linux platform provider, replace `PlatformToken` with that service and keep the vault only as a migration source
